# Time Commitment

The course requires a minimum of 100 hrs of work by each student over the six-week summer semester. The breakdown of this workload is detailed below:

-   Lectures: 1.5 hrs per class \* 15 class sessions = 22.5 hrs
-   Labs: 1.5 hrs per lab \* 9 lab sessions = 13.5 hrs
-   Readings/Assignments = 7 hrs per week \* 6 weeks = 42hrs
-   Final Project: 22 hrs per project \* 1 project = 22 hrs

Students learn and work in diverse ways, with differing styles, and at different speeds. The course workload detailed above approximates the time commitment for the course; but some students will require more time, and some less, depending upon a variety of factors. If you find that you are spending substantially more personal time than listed above and are, nonetheless, having difficulty understanding the material or completing assignments, then you should meet with the instructor and/or TA on a regular basis for suggestions and guidance. We do not want anyone to fall-behind in the course as it will become increasingly difficult to catch-up.

